  attachedPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d99e9125d5e5f574b86cb3f8c3e04de4, type: 3}
  logText: 'It has been a complicated week, but everything is more or less solved.
    They finally came to pick up Jeanne, and hopefully she will make it back to Earth
    without further complications. The physical pain she is feeling probably isn''t
    anything to be worried about, but every jump that we make takes its toll on our
    bodies. To prevent any major issues, we have decided to send her back with the
    rest of the team.


    This does mean that I will have to carry out the mission
    by myself, even if it technically goes against protocol. Gustave offered to join
    me, but I could tell he was tired and eager to get back home.


    As of right
    now, 7 of the 10 solar systems have been explored, and 2 more will be done by
    the end of the month. The rest of the crew have made amazing discoveries, and
    I simply can''t stand to be the only one who failed to complete their mission.
    There''s only three more planets to go, so I will push forward on my own.'
  orderFound: 0
  read: 0
